Yesterday I went MP on my production Alphaserver 1200, encouraged by 
recent reports of success (mostly in connection with PR 25599).  It's a 
routine I've gone through every three months or so since SMP was 
enabled, invariably ending in a hard system hang during some kind of 
heavy RAIDframe activity.

I've been through a full distribution build, as well as a complete 
build of the x.org sources, all while serving IMAP, and a PHP + MySQL 
IMP system.  Uptime has been far longer than I can ever remember on MP.

I would like to know where to send the Fat Tire and the Mirror Pond.

Dave



